# Java / Spring Boot Rules

- Follow the repository's established Java and Spring Boot versions; inspect before choosing versions.
- Keep controllers thin. Put business rules in service/domain layers and persistence logic behind repositories.
- Validate request data and enforce authorization server-side.
- Use explicit API DTOs instead of exposing persistence entities directly.
- Use database migrations for schema evolution; do not rely on automatic production schema creation.
- Add unit and relevant integration/contract tests. Do not claim tests pass unless run.
